# Normalise line endings.
#
# Without this, git on Windows checks files out as CRLF while Biome formats and
# expects LF. The result is that `npm run lint` passes on a file you just wrote
# and fails on the identical file after a `git checkout` — which is exactly how a
# lint failure reached main without anyone doing anything wrong.
#
# `eol=lf` forces LF in the working tree as well as in the repo, so git, Biome
# and CI all agree regardless of platform.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary assets must never be touched.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.webp binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ico binary
